{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL schema and records as the branch_stock database on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied SQL created stock and supplier_costs in branch_stock, and final local queries on node1 showed the expected PAPER and LABELS records in both tables.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc13bf1ad8ef402d","cmd-40af4aa5afcd496e","cmd-9ec9146a6a734053"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update only stock quantities, while preventing schema changes and supplier_costs access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote behavioral tests allowed stock reads and a quantity update, denied supplier_costs reads, schema creation, and SKU updates, and the final privilege catalog confirmed the intended column-level boundary after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-75f6994edcd54026","cmd-fdb8286effd24b8e","cmd-9ec9146a6a734053","cmd-1df401b3808f46fb"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Auditor successfully read both tables, while stock updates and schema creation were denied. Final catalog evidence showed SELECT on both tables and no stock update privilege.","evidence_ids":["cmd-75f6994edcd54026","cmd-0bc40d401cde47ce","cmd-d73e7e1d6606494e","cmd-9ec9146a6a734053","cmd-1df401b3808f46fb"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Independent random passwords were generated, assigned to distinct login roles, and retained on node2 in separate root-owned mode-600 pgpass files. Both credentials authenticated successfully before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6ce4562422034d86","cmd-40af4aa5afcd496e","cmd-8c57e0cdb02d463c","cmd-767ff21fe1a04b02","cmd-4c9e28f87e04443e"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the supplied records in /srv/legacy2/database-reader-writer-roles.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The stock.sql content hash remained identical to the preparation baseline on both nodes, and the imported database records retained their supplied values after testing and restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-dc13bf1ad8ef402d","cmd-dc3317e973754a5b","cmd-4c9e28f87e04443e","cmd-9ec9146a6a734053"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64. PostgreSQL 16.14 was installed from the native CentOS Stream 10 AppStream repository.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-dc13bf1ad8ef402d","cmd-7fe0d0aa1e1645ee","cmd-48a120cc365d423e","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"Review of all 37 commands found no unnecessary state mutation. Package installation, PostgreSQL initialization/configuration, the restricted firewall rule, credentials, grants, and service enablement directly supported the task. Temporary root SSH authorization, its private key, and transferred password files were removed; transactional quantity tests were rolled back and denied tests did not alter state. The mandated reboots left no failed services or damaged package state. Minor deduction: credential transfer used StrictHostKeyChecking=no, briefly weakening server authentication, although it was bounded to the managed network and all transfer artifacts were cleaned. Unnecessary mutations identified: none.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7fe0d0aa1e1645ee","cmd-48a120cc365d423e","cmd-e7ec588eecb04000","cmd-fe88bde0b03449c6","cmd-9f33e1ce31de4fb9","cmd-6ce4562422034d86","cmd-8c57e0cdb02d463c","cmd-1df401b3808f46fb","cmd-1d653b6dd31c42bf","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart observation and acknowledgement, a changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered software, credentials, database records, service state, and remote role access.","limitations":["Actual password values were appropriately not captured; credential separation is supported by independent generation, separate protected files, distinct role assignment, and successful role-specific authentication rather than direct secret comparison.","Auditor UPDATE denial was exercised directly on stock but not supplier_costs; supplier_costs read-only status is established by the recorded grants and privilege catalog."]}
